menu "IR playback (RMT TX)"

    config IR_PLAYBACK_TX_MEM_SYMBOLS
        int "RMT TX memory block size (symbols)"
        range 48 96
        default 48
        help
            Hardware FIFO owned by the TX channel. Must be even and at least
            SOC_RMT_MEM_WORDS_PER_CHANNEL (48 on the ESP32-C3). The copy encoder
            refills it in chunks, so it does not need to hold a whole frame.

    config IR_PLAYBACK_TX_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Transmission completion timeout (ms)"
        range 100 20000
        default 3000
        help
            Upper bound for one rmt_tx_wait_all_done() call. A single frame is
            never longer than about 300 ms, so 3 s only trips on a real fault.

endmenu
